===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Somebody who is [[force#Verb|forced]] to [[stand up]], for example, on a [[crowded]] [[bus#Noun|bus]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|month=September|author=Cecil J. Allen|title=Locomotive Running Past and Present|journal=Trains Illustrated|pages=430–431|text=Recently I received a letter from Mr. A. H. Maclean, who travelled north by the 11-coach "Flying Scotsman", and remarked that the train "was filled to capacity and we were forced to stand in the corridor"&mdash;for nearly 270 miles&mdash; [...] Obviously the diesel was working well below her load capacity on this schedule and some addition to the formation ought to have been made to accommodate the '''standees'''.}}
# A [[free-standing]], [[rigid]] [[print#Noun|print]] (usually [[life-sized]]), for instance of a [[celebrity]], often [[display#Verb|displayed]] for [[advertising]] and [[promotional]] purposes.
#: {{syn|en|cut-out}}
#: {{ux|en|He took a picture of me with a '''standee''' of [[Darth Vader]] at the premiere of ''[[w:Star Wars: Episode III – Revenge of the Sith|Star Wars: Episode III]]''.}}
# A [[board game]] piece made of [[cardboard]] inserted into a [[plastic]] base.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/386847/standies-and-what-to-do-about-them|date=2009-03-04|author=Martin Manning|work=BoardGameGeek|text=I've always found the best thing to do with '''standees''' is to stick a small strip of clear tape to the edge of the cardboard that will be inserted into the stand. This prevents the shredding/tearing problem.}}
# {{lb|en|military}} A kind of [[stackable]] [[bunk]] for sleeping.

